      "text": "We have the given equation: $|n + 6| = 2 - n$.\n\nIn order to avoid the absolute value symbol on the left-hand side, we can consider two cases:\nCase I: $n + 6 \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow n \\geq -6$\n\nIn this case, $|n + 6| = n + 6$. Thus, we'll have: $n + 6 = 2 - n$.\n\nNow, we solve for $n$: $2n = -4 \\Rightarrow n = -2$.\n\nCase II: $n + 6 < 0 \\Rightarrow n < -6$\n\nIn this case, $|n + 6| = -(n + 6)$. Thus, we'll have: $-(n + 6) = 2 - n$.\n\nThen, we solve for $n$: $-n - 6 = 2 - n$.\n\nCancelling the terms, we obtain $-6 = 2 \\Rightarrow n$ admits NO solution.\n\nTherefore, $n = \\boxed{-2}$.",
